# WHAT THE IMAGE BUILD MUST NOT CARRY. `server/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, so everything here is
# sent to the daemon on every build; a checkout on a machine that has built once holds ~600 MB of
# `build/` directories, against ~30 MB of actual sources. CI never noticed — a fresh checkout has
# none of them — which is exactly why this file is easy to forget and only bites locally.
#
# `.git` IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. Nothing in the build reads it today, but a build-identity plugin
# that stamps the commit into the binary does, and it is 8 MB.
**/build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
kotlin-js-store/
**/node_modules/
local.properties
*.iml
